# EXPERIMENT: MatrixPilot-style FIXED gain -- no dynamic-pressure schedule.
# RKT_QSCHED 0 makes the mixer run at a constant scale (MOT_GAIN_MAX); the aerodynamic moment
# then scales with real airspeed on its own, exactly like the flown MatrixPilot rocket. The
# question: does a fixed gain drive a 20-deg rail to vertical without oscillating at boost q?
RKT_QSCHED     0
MOT_GAIN_MAX   1.0
RKT_TILT_P     2.5
RKT_TILT_D     0.5
RKT_TILT_I     2.0
# spin damper: fixed mode runs the mixer at scale 1.0 vs ~0.135 at high q under the schedule,
# so the effective spin gain is ~7x higher -- drop 0.05 -> 0.006 to match the well-behaved level.
RKT_SPIN_DAMP  0.006
